    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. you mentioned \"transient populations\" and \"community factors\" being signals. specifically when looking at urban areas, how do shifts in the actual makeup of the population or changes in the types of local businesses (like a change in cultural or ethnic character of the shops) play into the stability score? does that usually correlate with higher risk for us?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
